  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">From Crisis to Care: A Healthcare Legacy For Vulnerable Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;Overall Objective: To provide essential healthcare and mental health support services to vulnerable individuals in crisis-affected communities&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Specific Objective 1: Displaced households (HHs), returnees, host communities, and remaining residents affected by the conflict have improved access to essential primary health care services while ensuring continuity of their medical care through PHCCs and MMUs in the South and Mount Lebanon.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Output 1.1: Address the most pressing health needs of displaced HHs, returnees, host communities, and remaining residents through the targeted PHCCs and MMUs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Output 1.2: Ensure access to basic paramedical needs to alleviate the burdens of the conflict on displaced HHs, returnees, host communities, and remaining residents.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Specific Objective 2: Displaced HHs, returnees, host communities, and remaining residents affected by the conflict gain improved access to essential mental health services, boosting resilience through PHCCs and Mobile Mental Health Units in the South and Mount Lebanon.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Output 2.1: Address the most pressing mental health needs of displaced HHs, returnees, host communities, and remaining residents through targeted PHCCs and Mobile Mental Health Units&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
